  "chapter": {
    "number": 63,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(64) For the end, a Psalm of David."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Hear my prayer, O God, when I make my petition to you; deliver my soul from fear of the enemy.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have sheltered me from the conspiracy of them that do wickedly; from the multitude of them that work iniquity;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "who have sharpened their tongues as a sword; they have bent their bow maliciously;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "to shoot in secret at the blameless; they will shoot him suddenly, and will not fear.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They have set up for themselves an evil matter, they have given counsel to hide snares; they have said, Who shall see them?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "They have searched out iniquity; they have wearied themselves with searching diligently, a man shall approach and the heart is deep,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and God shall be exalted, their wounds were caused by the weapon of the foolish children,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and their tongues have set him at nothing, all that saw them were troubled;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and every man was alarmed, and they related the works of God, and understood his deeds.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The righteous shall rejoice in the Lord, and hope on him, and all the upright in heart shall be praised.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": []
  },
